<description>
Fill black gaps with the unique known color from each cell's horizontal/vertical mirror orbit.

Input structure
The grid is an otherwise nonblack pattern with color 0 marking missing pixels. Nonblack cells reveal a horizontal reflection over the lower row band and a vertical reflection over the right column band.

Rule
Infer the row-reflection and column-reflection constants whose reflected nonblack pairs agree. For each black pixel, collect its row mirror, column mirror, and combined row+column mirror positions that stay in bounds; the known colors in that orbit must be unique, and every black pixel in the orbit is recolored to it.

Key insight
A gap can face another gap across one mirror axis, so the fill must use the full two-axis reflection orbit rather than a single reflected cell.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "grid with black mask pixels over a pattern symmetric by row reflection after a two-row prefix and by column reflection after a two-column prefix",
  "transform": "replace each black mask pixel with the unique nonblack color in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; preserve all visible pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x30 always
  output_pattern:
    description: dense pixel-level colorful pattern, no black, no tiling beyond symmetry
    colors: 5-7 distinct non-black colors
    symmetry: |
      double reflection with row_s=col_s=31 (axis between indices 15 and 16)
      rows 2-29 obey row[r] == row[31-r]; cols 2-29 obey col[c] == col[31-c]
      rows 0-1 and cols 0-1 are unpaired prefix strips (no mirror partner)
    adjacency_same_color_rate: ~36-40% per row/column [observed]
  mask:
    description: 3-4 axis-aligned rectangular black (color 0) regions erasing parts of the pattern
    component_count: 3-4
    component_shape: rectangular (rarely L-shaped from adjacent rects)
    component_size: 2-11 rows x 2-11 cols per block
    total_black_pct: 4-13% of grid
    solvability: every black cell must have >=1 non-black orbit partner under the double reflection
    placement: never in prefix corner (rows 0-1 AND cols 0-1 simultaneously); may touch prefix rows or cols but not both
  transform: fill each black cell with the unique non-black color from its {row-mirror, col-mirror, both-mirror} orbit

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Build output -- generate a 30x30 grid with 5-7 random non-black colors, enforcing double reflection (row_s=col_s=31). Fill the fundamental domain (rows 2-15, cols 2-15) randomly, mirror to get rows 2-29 x cols 2-29. Fill prefix rows 0-1 and cols 0-1 independently (random, no symmetry constraint).
    2. Place mask -- choose 3-4 non-overlapping rectangles (2-11 rows, 2-11 cols each), totaling 4-13% of grid. Ensure no rect covers the prefix corner (rows 0-1, cols 0-1). For each black cell, verify at least one orbit partner is NOT also black; if violated, shrink or shift the rect.
    3. Derive input -- copy the output, then zero out the masked rectangles.
```
</generation_spec>
